title: 'pallet-revive: drop cfg-gated host functions from the upload import allowlist'
doc:
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    Contracts that import the benchmark-only `noop` host function are now rejected at upload with
    `CodeRejected` on production runtimes. Previously such uploads were accepted, and the contract
    then trapped with `InvalidSyscall` as soon as it called `noop`. No working contract is
    affected, since calling that function could never succeed outside benchmarking builds.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `list_syscalls()` now respects each host function's `#[cfg]`, so builds without
    `runtime-benchmarks` no longer list `noop`. With `runtime-benchmarks`, `check_pvm_code` still
    accepts blobs importing `noop`, and its docs now say so. The unused `lookup_syscall_index` has
    been removed. The trace op list is unchanged.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive-proc-macro
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
